course: dictionary
lesson: 7069
title: Words for places outside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A patio is a flat, paved area next to a house. Paved means covered with flat stones or concrete, so the ground is hard and even. People use a patio for sitting, eating and relaxing outside.
explain: Read the words around patio to work out its meaning. «Ants follow smell trails to a crumb on the patio» tells you the patio is outside, where crumbs can fall from a picnic. The sentence «with space around it on soft ground, away from fences and patios» tells you a patio is a place near the house, like a fence is.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If patio means a flat, hard area by the house, then «away from fences and patios» still makes sense. That is a good sign you have the right meaning.
explain: Hard ground matters. «A trampoline throws you up, and you come down onto the patio» tells you the patio is hard, so a fall onto it can hurt badly. Patios can also be slippery when wet or icy, so take care when you walk on one.
fact: A patio is a flat, paved area next to a house.
fact: Families often have barbecues on the patio and put tables, chairs and plant pots there.
fact: Patio furniture means the tables, chairs and seats you keep on a patio.
fact: «Patio doors» are big glass sliding doors that open from the house onto the patio.
fact: Patios can be slippery when wet or icy, so walk carefully.
exercise: «Ants follow smell trails to a crumb on the patio.» Where is the crumb? | In a bedroom | Inside a cupboard | *Outside, on a flat paved area | Under the sea
exercise: What is a patio? | A deep hole dug for a pond | A kind of boat | *A flat, paved area next to a house | A tall tree in a garden
exercise: Which thing would you sensibly keep on a patio? | A hot air balloon | *Chairs and plant pots | Fish from the sea
test: What are «patio doors»? | Small doors for pets | Doors made of wood that lock from inside | Doors that lead to a cellar | *Big glass sliding doors that open onto a patio
test: Why should you take care on a patio in winter? | It has no light at night | *It can be slippery when wet or icy | It is full of sand | It is too soft to walk on
exam: «You come down onto the patio.» Why would landing on a patio hurt? | *It is hard, paved ground | It is soft like grass | It has a safety net | It is full of water
